Postgres housekeeping notes

After the analytics rewrite, three tables are unused. Confirm with `pg_stat_user_tables` that they have had zero sequential scans for 30 days, then drop the table in a transaction so you can roll back if a forgotten job complains:

```sql
BEGIN;
DROP TABLE legacy_events;
-- verify nothing screams
COMMIT;
```

Take a logical dump first. `pg_dump -t legacy_events` takes two minutes and has saved me twice.
